      "worked": "For a translation $a$ units right and $b$ units up, replace $x$ with $x-a$ and $y$ with $y-b$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x-a)(y-b)&=1\\\\xy-bx-ay+ab&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nComparing with $xy+2x-y=3$ gives\n$$\\begin{align*}-b&=2\\\\-a&=-1.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $a=1$ and $b=-2$. Checking the constant term,\n$$1-ab=1-(1)(-2)=3.$$\nTherefore, the translations were 1 unit right and 2 units down.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
